.TH AR01 1 "October 2026" "mc6801-tools" "mc6801-tools Manual"
.SH NAME
ar01 \- create and maintain libraries of MC6801 object files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ar01
.RB [ \- ]\fIkey\fP
.RI [ posname ]
.I archive
.RI [ file \&...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ar01
maintains archives (libraries) of object files produced by
.BR as01 (1).
.BR ld01 (1)
searches archives with its
.B \-l
option and links only the members that are needed.
The archive format is the standard Unix
.B !<arch>
format.
.PP
.I key
is one operation letter, optionally combined with modifier letters.
The leading
.B \-
is optional.
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.B r
Replace the named files in the archive, or add them at the end if they
are not already there.
Creates the archive if it does not exist.
.TP
.B q
Quick append: add the named files at the end without checking for
existing members.
.TP
.B d
Delete the named members.
.TP
.B m
Move the named members, by default to the end of the archive.
.TP
.B t
List the members, or only the named ones.
.TP
.B x
Extract the named members into the current directory, or all members if
none are named.
.TP
.B p
Write the contents of the named members (or all members) to standard
output.
.SH MODIFIERS
.TP
.B a
With
.B r
or
.BR m ,
place the files after member
.IR posname .
.TP
.BR b ", " i
With
.B r
or
.BR m ,
place the files before member
.IR posname .
.TP
.B c
Do not report when a new archive is created.
.TP
.B o
On extraction, give files the modification time recorded in the
archive.
.TP
.B u
With
.BR r ,
replace only members older than the named files.
.TP
.B v
Verbose: report each file added, replaced or extracted, and give a long
listing with
.BR t .
.TP
.B l
Accepted and ignored.
.TP
.B s
Add or update a
.B __.SYMDEF
member, an index of the symbols that each member exports, including
common blocks.
Once an archive has an index, later changes to the archive keep it up
to date.
.BR ld01 (1)
does not need the index; it reads every member\(aqs symbols directly.
Members that are not object files are reported and left out of the
index.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a library from three modules:
.PP
.RS
.B ar01 rc libnum.a one.o two.o three.o
.RE
.PP
List its contents in detail:
.PP
.RS
.B ar01 tv libnum.a
.RE
.PP
Link against it:
.PP
.RS
.B ld01 \-Cstart \-lnum \-T0x434c \-o main.aout main.o
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR as01 (1),
.BR ld01 (1),
.BR objdump01 (1)
.PP
The mc6801\-tools User\(aqs Manual
.RI ( mc6801\-tools\-manual.pdf ).
